---
description: Preserve canonical architecture and prevent parallel implementations
alwaysApply: true
---

Locate the existing canonical owner and trace the complete call path before
implementation. Check database functions, repositories, services, APIs, events,
authorization, organization and transaction boundaries.

Do not create duplicate domain models, validation, authorization, calculation,
status logic or local fallbacks. Do not replace a transaction with sequential
requests. Do not silently change public contracts. When duplicates exist,
choose the canonical owner, migrate callers, add tests and remove the old path.
